.TH MINIT 1 "1970-1-1" "v1.0" "Custom Scripts Manual"
.SH NAME
minit \- CMake project initializer and dependency manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B minit
\fIinit\fR|\fIinitialize\fR|\fInew\fR [\fB\-v\fR] \fIpath\fR [\fIpath\-options\fR]
.br
.B minit
\fIconf\fR|\fIconfigure\fR \fIpath\fR [\fB\-\-add\fR \fIdep\fR] [\fB\-\-remove\fR \fIdep\fR]
.br
.B minit
\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B minit
is a utility script for initializing and managing CMake projects. It creates
structured project directories with customizable CMake configurations, handles
dependency management through a simple interface, and generates configure
scripts for building.
.PP
The script operates in two primary modes:
.B init
(create new projects) and
.B conf
(manage existing project dependencies).
.SH INIT MODE
Creates a new CMake project structure at the specified path with configurable
options.
.TP
\fB\-v, \-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output during project creation.
.TP
\fB\-n, \-\-name \fINAME\fR
Set a custom project name (defaults to directory name).
.TP
\fB\-l, \-\-lib\fR
Mark the project as a library (enabled by default).
.TP
\fB\-b, \-\-no\-bin\fR
Disable binary/executable generation (enabled by default).
.TP
\fB\-c, \-\-config\fR
Generate a configure script for the project.
.TP
\fB\-\-cc\fR
Generate compile_commands.json for IDE integration.
.TP
\fB\-\-cxx\fR
Enable C++ support in addition to C.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-c\fR
Disable C language support.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-git\fR
Skip git repository initialization and .gitignore generation.
.TP
\fB\-\-tests\fR
Enable test framework structure (requires manual testing library setup).
.SH CONF MODE
Manages dependencies for an existing CMake project.
.TP
\fB\-\-add \fIdep\fR
Add a dependency to the 'deps' interface in CMakeLists.txt.
.TP
\fB\-\-remove \fIdep\fR
Remove a dependency from the 'deps' interface.
.SH FILES CREATED
When initializing a project,
.B minit
creates the following directory structure and files:
.TP
.I CMakeLists.txt
Main CMake configuration with customizable settings.
.TP
.I configure
Optional build configuration script (if \fB\-c\fR specified).
.TP
.I src/private/
Source directory with private headers subdirectory.
.TP
.I include/
Public headers directory (for libraries).
.TP
.I tests/
Test directory (if \fB\-\-tests\fR specified).
.TP
.I .gitignore
Git ignore file (if git enabled).
.SH CMake OPTIONS
The generated CMakeLists.txt includes several configurable options:
.TP
.B USE_CCACHE
Enable ccache for faster builds.
.TP
.B USE_LTO
Enable link-time optimization.
.TP
.B MARCH_NATIVE
Optimize for native architecture.
.TP
.B DO_INSTALL
Enable installation targets.
.TP
.B BUILD_SHARED/BUILD_STATIC
Control library type (for library projects).
.SH DEPENDENCY MANAGEMENT
Dependencies are managed through the
.B deps
interface target in CMakeLists.txt. Use the
.B conf
mode to add or remove dependencies between the
.B @DEPS_START@
and
.B @DEPS_END@
markers.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a new library project with tests:
.RS
.PP
minit init ./myproject \-\-tests
.RE
.PP
Create a binary-only project with custom name:
.RS
.PP
minit init ./project \-\-no\-lib \-\-name "myapp"
.RE
.PP
Add a dependency to existing project:
.RS
.PP
minit conf ./myproject \-\-add "Threads::Threads"
.RE
.PP
Remove a dependency:
.RS
.PP
minit conf ./myproject \-\-remove "Threads::Threads"
.RE
.SH NOTES
The script uses portable sed commands compatible with both GNU sed and BSD sed.
.PP
When enabling tests, users must manually configure their preferred testing
library (e.g., Google Test, Catch2) in the generated tests/CMakeLists.txt.
.PP
The configure script generated by \fB\-c\fR supports common CMake generators
(Ninja, Unix Makefiles) and provides a convenient wrapper for build
configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.MR cmake 1 ,
.MR sed 1 ,
.MR git 1 ,
.MR bash 1
.SH BUGS
The script assumes a POSIX-compliant environment with bash 4.0 or newer.
Multiple path handling in init mode may have unexpected behavior with complex
option combinations.
